unit ModuleHelper3;

/// Two `uses` hops from Modules.a24, which is the whole reason this file exists.
///
/// ⚠️ Modules.a24 imports ModuleHelper, and ModuleHelper imports this. Nothing
/// else in the corpus is a chain: every other fixture is a leaf, and the two
/// large multi-module programs -- `algc` and the Lox interpreter -- are stars,
/// where the root imports every other file directly.
///
/// The `test` block below is the point. `--test` used to resolve every test
/// from the root file's environment, which reaches the root's own names and its
/// imports' -- and `uses` is not transitive, so this one was reported as FAIL
/// with `Undefined variable ''...''` naming *itself*. The program ran correctly
/// in every path; only the runner was wrong, and only at depth two or more.

function Helper3Peek(): Integer;
begin
    Exit 3;
end

test 'A Test Two Uses Hops From The Root Still Runs';
begin
    AssertEqual(3, Helper3Peek());
end
